Falsifies `system_tests::user::non_volatile_memory_express_tests::a_client_stages_in_the_window_its_badge_names`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect is the NVMe server staging every request in window 0, whatever its badge names: the
shared transfer region the per-client windows replaced (milestone 834 (ioping on nife and Linux),
calef's "Per-client window", 2026-10-18 UTC). A known badge is still admitted and an unknown one
still refused, so the server comes up and answers every verb; only where the bytes go is wrong.

The test needs an NVMe controller attached, which `cargo xtask test` does on every test leg
(`NIFE_NVME`), so this replays with no extra setup.

Expected to fail: "byte 0 of the disk tree's read came back wrong". The installer's write stages
from window 0, which still holds 0x11, so 0x11 is what reaches block 41; the disk tree's read then
lands in window 0 too, and window 2 still holds the 0xaa the test filled it with.
Replayed 2026-10-18 (UTC), aarch64: failed at exactly that assertion.

